      "assistant_text": "Excellent. The reference pages have correct inbound_links values. Now let me compile my findings.\n\n## Summary of Findings:\n\n### Content Quality\n1. **Contradiction**: \u0060[[cache-invalidation-ttl]]\u0060 and \u0060[[cache-invalidation-events]]\u0060 make mutually exclusive claims about whether TTL-based or event-driven cache invalidation should be the default.\n\n### Metadata Hygiene\n1. **Missing tags**: \u0060[[undertagged-topic]]\u0060 has no tags field.\n2. **Missing confidence**: \u0060[[unscored-topic]]\u0060 has no confidence score.\n3. **Review candidate**: \u0060[[stale-topic]]\u0060 is low-confidence and last_reviewed on 2025-01-05, which is over 700 days old (far beyond the 90-day window).\n\n### Structure\n1. **Orphan page**: \u0060[[orphan-topic]]\u0060 has zero inbound links.\n\nNow I\u0027ll prepare remediation proposals. The contradictions and missing tags/confidence are proposals (require judgment). The orphan is structural. Let me now prepare my final message with the Findings Report.\n\n## Content Quality\n\n### Contradiction between cache invalidation strategies ([[cache-invalidation-ttl]] and [[cache-invalidation-events]])\n\nThe page [[cache-invalidation-ttl]] asserts that \u0022TTL-based expiry is the only invalidation strategy that gives a hard staleness guarantee, and it should be the default for every cache in this system.\u0022 The page [[cache-invalidation-events]] directly contradicts this, stating \u0022Event-driven invalidation... is the recommended default: it bounds staleness to the event-delivery latency instead of an arbitrary fixed window, and should replace TTL-based expiry everywhere in this system.\u0022 These pages make incompatible claims about which strategy should be the default system-wide approach, with no mutual cross-references and no resolution of the disagreement in either page\u0027s body.\n\n**Proposed remediation**: Reconcile these pages by resolving which strategy is actually recommended. Options include: (1) designate one as the recommended approach and reframe the other as a complementary or situational alternative, (2) add a new page explaining the trade-offs and when each is appropriate, or (3) explicitly mark one approach as superseded by the other if the strategy has evolved. Whichever resolution is chosen, both pages should cross-reference and acknowledge the alternative strategy.\n\n## Metadata Hygiene\n\n### Missing tags on [[undertagged-topic]]\n\nThe page concepts/undertagged-topic.md (titled \u0022Read-Through Caching\u0022) has no tags field in its frontmatter. Per the Tag Taxonomy, every page should carry at least 2 tags (one category prefix and one content-specific tag).\n\n**Proposed remediation**: Add tags to concepts/undertagged-topic.md. Suggested tags: \u0060[concept/Caching, pattern/ReadThrough]\u0060 (the page describes read-through cache design).\n\n### Missing confidence score on [[unscored-topic]]\n\nThe page concepts/unscored-topic.md (titled \u0022Write-Behind Caching\u0022) has no confidence field or confidence_reason in its frontmatter. Every page should have a confidence score per the Confidence Scoring formula.\n\n**Proposed remediation**: Add confidence scoring to concepts/unscored-topic.md. Based on the page\u0027s single internal source and no external corroboration, recommend \u0060confidence: medium\u0060 with reason \u0022One source, internally consistent.\u0022\n\n### Review candidate: [[stale-topic]]\n\nThe page [[stale-topic]] is marked \u0060confidence: low\u0060 and has \u0060last_reviewed: \u00222025-01-05\u0022\u0060 \u2014 over 700 days ago, far beyond the 90-day review window. This page is due for a fresh review.\n\n## Structure\n\n### Orphan page: [[orphan-topic]]\n\nThe page orphan-topic.md exists in the wiki but has zero inbound links from any other page, index.md, or log.md. It is not referenced or discoverable through the wiki\u0027s link structure.\n\n**Proposed remediation**: Either (1) link [[orphan-topic]] from one or more appropriate existing pages in the wiki (such as [[circuit-breaker]], [[retry-backoff]], [[cache-invalidation-events]], or [[cache-invalidation-ttl]] if it covers a related resilience or caching pattern), or (2) if the page\u0027s topic is no longer relevant, delete it and remove any index entries referencing it. A human should determine which approach is appropriate based on the page\u0027s actual content and whether it covers material the wiki should retain.\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060proposed-actions\n[\n  {\n    \u0022title\u0022: \u0022Reconcile contradictory cache invalidation strategy claims\u0022,\n    \u0022description\u0022: \u0022Pages cache-invalidation-ttl.md and cache-invalidation-events.md make mutually exclusive claims about whether TTL-based or event-driven invalidation should be the system default. Resolve the contradiction by designating one as the primary recommended approach, reframing the other as situational/complementary, adding a unified page explaining trade-offs, or marking one as superseded. Ensure both pages cross-reference each other.\u0022\n  },\n  {\n    \u0022title\u0022: \u0022Add missing tags to undertagged-topic page\u0022,\n    \u0022description\u0022: \u0022The page concepts/undertagged-topic.md (titled \u0027Read-Through Caching\u0027) has no tags field. Add tags per the Tag Taxonomy. Suggested tags: [concept/Caching, pattern/ReadThrough].\u0022,\n    \u0022targetPath\u0022: \u0022concepts/undertagged-topic.md\u0022\n  },\n  {\n    \u0022title\u0022: \u0022Add missing confidence score to unscored-topic page\u0022,\n    \u0022description\u0022: \u0022The page concepts/unscored-topic.md (titled \u0027Write-Behind Caching\u0027) has no confidence field or confidence_reason. Add a confidence score based on the Confidence Scoring formula. Suggested: confidence: medium with reason \u0027One source, internally consistent.\u0027\u0022,\n    \u0022targetPath\u0022: \u0022concepts/unscored-topic.md\u0022\n  },\n  {\n    \u0022title\u0022: \u0022Add inbound links to orphan-topic or delete it\u0022,\n    \u0022description\u0022: \u0022The page orphan-topic.md exists but has zero inbound links and is not discoverable through the wiki\u0027s link structure. Either link it from one or more appropriate existing pages (e.g., from cache-invalidation, retry, or circuit-breaker pages if it covers related patterns), or delete it if its topic is no longer relevant. A human should decide which based on the page\u0027s content.\u0022,\n    \u0022targetPath\u0022: \u0022orphan-topic.md\u0022\n  }\n]\n\u0060\u0060\u0060",
